diff --git a/studio-core/docs/phase-project-simplify-actor-20261109.md b/studio-core/docs/phase-project-simplify-actor-20261109.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2a87d9a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/studio-core/docs/phase-project-simplify-actor-20261109.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Project consolidation and actor display refinement
+
+2026-11-09. Source baseline: private Site v105, d022030ed03151323202ab4fcea6da351241fa95.
+
+## Scope and decisions
+
+The owner asked to consolidate creative work into projects, remove separate management/planning/sound sidebar entries and review/tasks/production/delivery product destinations, then refine actor presentation. The dashboard now shows only recent story/document records; retired task/review links are not rendered, and filtered pages retain their load-more action. The left sidebar now contains dashboard, projects, actors and materials, with connection at the bottom. Projects expose story, episodes, storyboard, prompts, roles/scenes, relations, novel outline, planning and sound.
+
+Old review/task links return to creative work. Production/delivery bookmarks preserve the recovery surface when their existing session-scoped uncertain-write receipt is present, including when browser storage is inaccessible. Records, APIs, adoption rules and private access remain unchanged.
+
+Sound mounts the existing native sound library inside the project page, using the existing Shadow DOM module and API. It is honestly identified as the account sound library; no unsupported project binding is inferred. Draft and busy state feed the shell navigation guard, and disposal stops playback.
+
+The actor's original stays sharp and fully contained. The background uses that exact same displayed image, enlarged and offset, with a brighter soft-focus layer so face/environment colors remain recognizable. Full biography remains below the image. The actor switch uses a people icon rather than a dropdown chevron.
+
+Short authored bracket annotations render as restrained gold/teal/lilac/rose tags. The optional Markdown transform is display-only and skips code, links, images, raw HTML scopes, nested brackets and protected media placeholders. Editors retain exact source text. Tag light follows the existing pause control and reduced-motion preference.
+
+## Acceptance and negative cases
+
+- Single left navigation; no duplicate management/sound/planning sidebar links or separate review/tasks/production/delivery menu items.
+- All nine project destinations remain peer-level and use the existing dirty/busy guard.
+- Legacy uncertain handoff receipts remain recoverable; no data deletion, automatic adoption or permissions expansion.
+- Native sound controls stay in the current page, retain draft on cancelled navigation and permit leaving after explicit discard/clear.
+- Same src for actor background and foreground; foreground filter remains none; source does not get cropped to a fake cutout.
+- Bracket tags in display only, safe Markdown unchanged by default, labels wrap on narrow screens and pause stops their animation.
+- Owner isolation, original asset bytes, CAS/idempotency and errors/retry remain existing contracts.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- TypeScript check passed.
+- Full Site tests passed 879/879. Actor/Markdown, routing and sound focused checks passed 81/81 before the final full run.
+- Core mandatory review passed 161/161.
+- Browser: desktop + 390px actor layout, exact same-image src, clear original filter, color tags and paused animation verified; editor source still contains original brackets.
+- Browser: native sound loaded in the project page; unsaved upload description triggered the shell leave guard, cancelling retained exact input, clearing the isolated draft allowed navigation. Local audio data endpoints are not provided by the preview fixture; real-owner list readback remains a post-deploy check.
+- Complete final build passed. Compiled Worker smoke verified native sound module routes, owner isolation and migration/backup behavior; source-readiness returned complete. Deployment receipt is recorded in the root release evaluation.
+
+No production content was written during UI testing; the edited character was explicitly labelled FIXTURE in the local test database.
